# Free double-coset count: #(Hbackslash M/K)·|K|=[M:H]

Theorem statement: `Subgroup.card_orbitRelQuotient_mul_card_eq_index`
(`5c45036a-fa78-5e04-9231-abdaa4f44270`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `499349aa-7fe9-5213-80bc-5e6fd1b94016`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $M$ be a group and let $H$ and $K$ be subgroups of $M$. Assume that no nontrivial element of $K$
is conjugate into $H$: for all $g, x \in M$, if $x \in K$ and $g^{-1} x g \in H$, then $x = 1$. Then
the product of the number of orbits of $H$ acting by left translation on the left-coset space $M /
K$ — that is, the cardinality of the quotient of $M/K$ by the orbit relation of the $H$-action,
which is the double-coset space $H \backslash M / K$ — with the cardinality of $K$ equals the index
of $H$ in $M$. All three cardinalities are `Nat.card`, so each infinite set contributes the value
$0$ and the identity holds degenerately when $K$, the double-coset space or $M/H$ is infinite; in
particular no finiteness hypothesis is imposed on $M$, $H$ or $K$.

This is the elementary double-coset count underlying the Bass–Serre analysis of subgroups of free
products: a subgroup $H$ meeting no conjugate of a factor $K$ acts on the coset tree with the type
of $K$-vertices contributing $[M:H]/|K|$ orbits. It is used in the construction of free bases, for
subgroups of free products of groups
([`Monoid.CoprodI.nonempty_freeGroupBasis_fin_kuroshRank`]
(thm.html#Monoid.CoprodI.nonempty_freeGroupBasis_fin_kuroshRank))
and for subgroups of $\mathrm{SL}_2$ modulo centre generated by elements of prescribed trace
(`Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup.nonempty_freeGroupBasis_map_quotient_center_of_forall_trace_ne`)

